1
00:00:00,088 --> 00:00:04,408
Every system starts generic. — Yours does not have to stay that way.

2
00:00:07,889 --> 00:00:12,823
Six steps, and nothing is written until the last one.

3
00:00:12,823 --> 00:00:17,844
Pick what the practice actually is.

4
00:00:17,844 --> 00:00:26,531
More than one is fine. The first one leads where packs disagree.

5
00:00:26,531 --> 00:00:29,951
Then the step that matters.

6
00:00:29,951 --> 00:00:35,253
Twenty-three things to create. Four already there.

7
00:00:35,253 --> 00:00:37,512
And two it refuses to touch.

8
00:00:37,512 --> 00:00:42,382
You changed the annual physical to forty minutes. It stays forty minutes.

9
00:00:42,382 --> 00:00:46,332
A pack never restores its own version over an edit you made.

10
00:00:46,418 --> 00:00:50,918
Configured, not overwritten. — Your edits outrank the vendor’s defaults.
